menu "NeuroClaw-ESP"

    config NEUROCLAW_TASK_STACK
        int "Brain task stack (bytes)"
        default 8192
        range 6144 32768

    config NEUROCLAW_HISTORY
        int "Messages kept after the system prompt"
        default 16
        range 4 64
        help
            The conversation is saved to sessions/telegram.json of the
            workspace after every turn and read back at boot.

    config NEUROCLAW_MAX_ROUNDS
        int "LLM rounds per owner message"
        default 4
        range 1 8
        help
            A round is one LLM call; tool calls start another. After this many
            the owner is told the request was not finished.

    config NEUROCLAW_HEARTBEAT_MIN
        int "Heartbeat interval (minutes, 0 = off)"
        default 30
        range 0 1440
        help
            As the Go NeuroClaw's heartbeat (default 30): every so often the
            brain reads HEARTBEAT.md of its workspace and, if it lists tasks,
            checks them; a reply of HEARTBEAT_OK is not sent to the owner.

    config NEUROCLAW_SEND_FILE_MAX
        int "Largest file send_file sends (bytes)"
        default 10485760
        range 1024 52428800
        help
            The file is streamed from flash to Telegram, so this is not bounded
            by RAM; Telegram takes documents up to 50 MB, photos up to 10 MB.

    config NEUROCLAW_POLL_S
        int "Telegram long-poll timeout (s)"
        default 25
        range 1 50

    config NEUROCLAW_HTTP_MAX
        int "Largest HTTP reply kept (bytes)"
        default 65536
        range 8192 524288
        help
            A larger reply is dropped, never cut: a cut JSON reply could parse
            into something the model did not say.

endmenu
